>
  <p>
    Summer is peak moving season in Bristol. Longer days, better weather and the school holidays make June to September the busiest months for house moves across the city. If you're planning a move this summer, clearing out before you go can save you hundreds on removal costs and make the whole process less stressful.
  </p>

  <h2>Why Clear Out Before You Move</h2>
  <p>
    Most removal companies charge by volume or by the time it takes to load. Every item you move costs money — and moving things you don't want to the new property just delays the problem. A clearance before moving day means:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Lower removal costs</strong> — fewer items means a smaller van and less loading time</li>
    <li><strong>Faster move</strong> — the removal team works through your belongings more quickly</li>
    <li><strong>Fresh start</strong> — arrive at your new home with only what you actually want</li>
    <li><strong>Deposit protection</strong> — landlords deduct for items left behind</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to Clear Before Moving</h2>
  <p>Walk through each room and ask: am I going to use this in the new home? If the answer is no, it goes. Common items to clear before a move:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Old or worn furniture you're replacing at the new property</li>
    <li>Loft contents — boxes that haven't been opened since the last move</li>
    <li>Garden items — broken furniture, old pots, accumulated green waste</li>
    <li>Garage and shed contents — tools, paint, chemicals, broken equipment</li>
    <li>Appliances you're upgrading — old washing machines, fridges, cookers</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Timing Your Clearance</h2>
  <p>
    The best approach is to book a clearance <strong>2-3 weeks before your moving date</strong>. This gives you time to sort through everything at your own pace, set aside items for the move, and have us collect the rest. We can work around your schedule — evenings and weekends are available.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're on a tighter timeline, we also offer same-day and next-day clearance. In summer, our diary fills up quickly, so <a href="/contact/">booking early</a> is always advisable.
  </p>

  <h2>End-of-Tenancy Clearances</h2>
  <p>
    If you're a tenant, the stakes are higher. Landlords and letting agents will deduct from your deposit for any items left in the property, garden or loft. Bristol's rental market is competitive and many tenants lose hundreds of pounds to unnecessary deductions. Our <a href="/house-clearance/end-of-tenancy-clearance/">end-of-tenancy clearance</a> service ensures the property is completely cleared, clean and ready for inspection.
  </p>

  <h2>Downsizing? We Can Help</h2>
  <p>
    Moving to a smaller property is increasingly common in Bristol, whether you're an empty-nester moving from a family home or relocating to a more manageable space. <a href="/house-clearance/downsizing-clearance/">Downsizing clearances</a> require careful planning — deciding what fits, what goes to family, what's donated and what's disposed of. We work alongside you, handling the physical work while you make the decisions.
  </p>

  <h2>Book Your Summer Clearance</h2>
  <p>
    Summer slots book up fast. Call us on <strong>0117 123 4567</strong> or <a href="/contact/">get a free quote</a> today. Send us WhatsApp photos of what needs clearing for the fastest response.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
